sub:assertion {
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/thompson1917-ch12-03> delphi:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/thompson1917-ch12-03--grok> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/thompson1917-ch12-03--grok> a delphi:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Grok 4.7 on thompson1917-ch12-03: partially-resolvable, resolvability 0.55" ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/dataset-resolvability-0.2.0> ;
    delphi:assessmentType "dataset-resolvability/0.2.0" ;
    delphi:hasScore "0.549"^^xsd:double ;
    delphi:hasVerdict "partially-resolvable" ;
    delphi:hasConfidence "0.64"^^xsd:double ;
    dct:description "Curvature direction and closeness to a minimal surface are well-defined measurements, and the side the living tissue occupied is known for both groups. The necessary tomographic archives exist but are sparse, so a test would cover a few genera rather than chambered foraminifera and cephalopods at large. Segmentation is routine once scans are in hand, yet assembling a balanced sample would take specialist effort beyond a quick survey." ;
    rdfs:comment "Proposed test with existing data: Segment septal surfaces from micro-CT of chambered foraminifera and Nautilus, record the sign of curvature relative to the aperture, and compare each septum with the minimal surface spanning the same suture. Support would be outward convexity in foraminifera, outward concavity in Nautilus, and area close to the minimum; a systematic departure toward thicker, non-minimal septa, or curvature unrelated to which side was loaded, would refute the paired claim." ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-resolvability-assessor-grok-4.7-high-fast> ;
    delphi:evidenceAgainst "Public volumetric scans of septate foraminifera and nautiloids number in the tens, not a broad taxonomic sample.", "Minimal-area agreement can be produced by several loading histories, so curvature sign is clearer than the pressure story." ;
    delphi:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/thompson1917-ch12-03--grok--dataset-1>, <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/thompson1917-ch12-03--grok--dataset-2> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/thompson1917-ch12-03--grok--operationalizability> a delphi:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Operationalizability of thompson1917-ch12-03 by Grok 4.7: 0.75" ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/dataset-resolvability-0.2.0-operationalizability> ;
    delphi:assessmentType "dataset-resolvability/0.2.0/operationalizability" ;
    delphi:hasScore "0.75"^^xsd:double ;
    dct:isPartOf <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/thompson1917-ch12-03--grok> ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-resolvability-assessor-grok-4.7-high-fast> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/thompson1917-ch12-03> delphi:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/thompson1917-ch12-03--grok--operationalizability> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/thompson1917-ch12-03--grok--data-existence> a delphi:LLMClaimAssessment ;
